  "answer_markdown": "The Mistral documentation does not specify the maximum number of web pages that MistralAI-User may visit for a single user request in Vibe. It also does not directly address a per-minute rate limit for web page visits [1, 3, 5].\n\nHowever, the sources mention general rate limits that apply to API requests, tokens, and specific functionalities, such as:\n\n- Rate limits vary by subscription tier and model, including requests per second and tokens per minute [2, 7, 8].\n- The API returns a `429 Too Many Requests` error when rate limits are exceeded [2, 11].\n\nTo check your current rate limits, you can visit the [limits page](https://admin.mistral.ai/plateforme/limits) or the [Admin Panel > API > Limits](https://admin.mistral.ai/plateforme/limits) [2, 7].\n\nSince the documentation does not provide the specific details for web page visits, this question cannot be answered with the provided sources.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "MistralAI-User is for user actions in Vibe. When users ask Vibe a question, it may visit a web page to help answer and include a link to the source in its response."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Rate limits vary by subscription tier and model. When exceeded, the API returns `429 Too Many Requests`."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Work can browse the internet in real time and read specific web pages as part of a task."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "Open URL fetches only the single page at the URL you provide. It doesn't crawl the entire site or follow links."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "Rate limits apply at the Workspace level and are shared across all API keys in that Workspace."
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "quote": "Completion rate limits are listed per model and include: Tokens per minute: the token throughput limit for the model."
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "quote": "You have exceeded the rate limit for your subscription tier."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": true
}

