{
  "answer_markdown": "Some common use cases for fine-tuning a model instead of relying on prompting include:\n\n1. **Customizing the model to generate responses in a specific format and tone.**\n   - This is particularly useful for applications like legal copilots where structured, well-sourced, and professionally formatted responses are required. Fine-tuning can ensure that the model adheres to these requirements without needing a complex prompt, thereby saving tokens and reducing costs.\n\n2. **Specializing the model for a specific topic or domain.**\n   - Fine-tuning allows the model to improve its performance on domain-specific tasks, such as legal translation. For example, fine-tuning a model on the [Multi EURLEX](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2109.00904) dataset significantly improved the translation of legal terminology, resulting in a 94% preference for the fine-tuned model over the base model in legal expert evaluations.\n\n3. **Improving model performance through distillation from a stronger model.**\n   - This approach involves training a smaller model to mimic the behavior of a larger, more capable model. This can reduce costs and latency while maintaining performance, as demonstrated in the example of fine-tuning `mistral-small` using `mistral-large` as a teacher model.\n\n4. **Enhancing model performance to mimic the behavior of a model with a complex prompt.**\n   - Fine-tuning can achieve similar results to a complex prompt without the need for the prompt itself, saving tokens and reducing associated costs.\n\n5. **Reducing cost and latency.**\n   - Using a small, efficient fine-tuned model can be more cost-effective and faster than relying on a larger model or complex prompts.\n\n6. **Teaching new facts and information to the model.**\n   - Fine-tuning can be used to impart new knowledge or workflows to the model, such as advanced tools or complicated processes.\n\n7. **Developing specialized applications like legal summarization, contract analysis, and legal drafting.**\n   - Fine-tuning allows for the creation of models tailored to specific applications, enabling more efficient and effective human-AI collaboration.\n\nFor developers interested in fine-tuning, Mistral provides a [fine-tuning API](https://docs.mistral.ai/resources/cookbooks?useCase=Finetuning) and a [quick guide on building applications with a custom model](https://docs.mistral.ai/resources/deprecated/customization#overview).\n\n```\n\n```\n```\n\n",
