message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To investigate who deleted conversations, the administrator would look for the event type `le_chat.conversation.deleted` from le Chat events [3]. They can narrow the results to a specific human user by using the `actor_user_uuid` parameter [1, 5]. The default number of entries returned per request is 20 [1, 5].\n\nHere is an example of how to query audit logs programmatically:\n\n```\nGET /v1/admin/audit-logs?event_type=le_chat.conversation.deleted&actor_user_uuid=<specific_user_uuid>\n```\n\nReplace `<specific_user_uuid>` with the UUID of the human user [5].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Audit log entries are generated from the Admin API schema and dashboard audit log constants. Metadata fields vary by event and resource type."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Use these query parameters with the [Admin API audit logs endpoint](https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/beta/admin/audit-logs)."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Records when a le Chat conversation is deleted."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "Filter logs by the UUID of the user who performed the action."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "GET /v1/admin/audit-logs"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

